# Cloudflare header rules for the web build (Workers Static Assets).
#
# Cloudflare has no server config, so the policies docker/nginx.conf applies to
# this same build are restated here. Read that file alongside this one before
# editing.
#
# THE RULE THAT SHAPES THIS FILE: when several rules match a request, Cloudflare
# APPENDS their values into one header rather than letting the more specific rule
# win. A `/*` rule and an `/assets/*` rule both setting Cache-Control produced
# `no-cache, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable` on hashed
# assets, where `no-cache` wins and the year-long cache never applied. So no
# header may be set by two rules that can match the same path. `/*` therefore
# carries only the headers that are genuinely universal, and every Cache-Control
# lives on a specific path.
#
# The same append behaviour is why the JupyterLite CSP is NOT here: a second
# policy does not replace the app policy, and a comma-joined CSP is enforced as
# multiple policies whose intersection applies — leaving JupyterLab's inline
# bootstrap blocked by the app policy regardless. That prefix is handled in
# workers/web/src/index.ts, which can replace the header outright.
#
# Two deliberate differences from nginx.conf — not drift:
#
# 1. connect-src drops http://localhost:*, http://127.0.0.1:* and their ws://
#    forms. nginx.conf and the Dockerfile both warn that those allowances exist
#    for the local/single-user Docker image: in a browser "localhost" is the
#    visitor's machine, so on a public host they let the served JS probe each
#    visitor's own loopback. This deployment is public.
# 2. The __GEOLIBRE_*__ placeholders that entrypoint.sh substitutes at container
#    boot are resolved to literals here. As written that means no Clerk and no
#    Auth0 sign-in gate; enabling either also means adding its origins to
#    script-src/frame-src below by hand.
#
# Keep both the hosted relay and this fork's self-hosted relay. The directive
# carries a bare `https:` but no bare `wss:`, so omitting the second origin made
# the app advertise collaboration while the browser blocked its WebSocket.

# Universal headers only. No Cache-Control here: it would append to every
# per-path rule below and `no-cache` would win over all of them.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https: data: blob: wss://collab.geolibre.app wss://geolibre-collab.jonasnguyen886.workers.dev; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data: https://js.arcgis.com/; script-src 'self' blob: 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/ https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/pyodide/ https://js.arcgis.com/ https://accounts.google.com https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/; child-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://www.google.com; frame-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://www.google.com; worker-src blob: 'self'

# Vite content-hashes every file it emits here, so a redeploy mints new
# filenames and these are safe to pin for a year. Scoped to the directory rather
# than to file extensions the way nginx.conf's regex location is: an extension
# rule would also match /sw.js, and pinning the service worker for a year strands
# a stale one that the autoUpdate flow can never replace.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Stable filenames that change contents on a redeploy — they must revalidate or
# a visitor keeps running the previous build.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/plugins/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Deployment configuration, read at load before the bundle. Workbox already
# excludes it from the precache; keep it off the HTTP cache too.
/geolibre-runtime-config.js
  Cache-Control: no-store

# nginx's default mime.types has no .webmanifest entry, so nginx.conf sets this
# by hand. Set it here too rather than relying on type inference.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
